Run Multiple Containers using Docker Compose
We will run:
Web server (nginx) 
Another container (same image) 
Step 1 — Create docker-compose.yml
		notepad docker-compose.yml
Write this and save it.
version: '3'
services:
  web1:
    image: nginx
    ports:
      - "8081:80"
  web2:
    image: nginx
    ports:
      - "8082:80"

Step 2 — Run Compose (up)
docker-compose up -d
Step 3 — Check running containers
docker ps
Step 4 — Verify in browser
Open:
http://localhost:8081
http://localhost:8082
Both will show nginx page
Step 5 — Stop all containers
docker-compose down



